<title>GERMANY: TABLE-German May adj numbers in work fall.</title>
<headline>TABLE-German May adj numbers in work fall.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistics Office reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p>PAN-GERMAN NUMBERS IN WORK		 May 97   Apr 97   May 96</p>
<p> Number in work (1)(unadj, million)    33.865   33.862   34.414</p>
<p> Number in work (1)(seas adj, million) 33.961   33.986   34.513</p>
<p> Number in work (2)(seas adj, million) 34.006   34.031   34.571</p>
<p>WEST GERMAN</p>
<p> Number in work (unadj,million)	  27.826   27.798   28.197</p>
<p> Number in work (seas adj, million)    27.871   27.879   28.246</p>
<p>EAST GERMAN</p>
<p> Number in work (unadj, million)	  6.100    6.104    6.289</p>
<p> Number in work (seas adj, million)     6.135    6.152    6.325</p>
<p>NOTE - Pan-German figure marked (1) refers to people living in Germany. Those marked (2), as well as all the west and east German figures, refer to commuters who work in the respective regions but do not necessarily live in Germany.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
